.\" likeos-install.1 - manual page for likeos-install, the text-mode
.\" installer.
.\"
.\" The troff source.  man(1) on this system reads pre-formatted pages; the
.\" installed copy is res/man-live/likeos-install.1 (the live medium only),
.\" rendered from this file by "make installer-manpages" (mk/installer.mk).
.\"
.\" Copyright (C) 2026 The LikeOS Project
.TH LIKEOS-INSTALL 1 "November 2026" "LikeOS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
likeos-install \- install LikeOS on a disk, in a text terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B likeos-install
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-reboot ]
.br
.B likeos-install \-\-answers
.I file
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-reboot ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B likeos-install \-\-list\-disks
.br
.B likeos-install \-\-reset\-tty
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B likeos-install
installs LikeOS from the medium it was started from onto a disk of the
computer: it partitions the disk (or uses a partition of it), creates the
file systems, unpacks the system image, sets up the new system \(em language,
time zone, keyboard, computer name, the root password and a user account
\(em, installs the boot loader on the EFI system partition, registers it
with the firmware, and restarts the computer into the installed system.
.PP
It is the text-mode counterpart of the graphical installer,
.BR likeos-installer (1),
and does the same work through the same installer library; the installation
medium offers it when the graphical installer cannot run (a computer whose
graphics do not work), and it runs in any terminal, also over a serial line
or
.BR ssh (1).
It must run as root.
.SS Interactive installation
Started without
.BR \-\-answers ,
.B likeos-install
asks the questions of the graphical installer, one at a time: the language
of the installed system and the format of dates and times, the disk to
install on (to be erased completely, or one of its partitions), the time
zone, the keyboard layouts (up to four), the computer's name, the root
password, and the name, user name and password of the account to sign in
with; then it shows a summary and asks for a last confirmation before anything is
written to the disk.
Typing
.B back
(or
.BR < )
at a question returns to the one before; Ctrl-C or the end of the input
cancels the installation \(em until the confirmation nothing has been
changed.
On a terminal the progress of the installation is a bar that redraws itself;
when the standard input or output is not a terminal every question reads one
line and the progress is printed line by line, so the program can be driven
by another program or logged.
.SS Unattended installation
With
.B \-\-answers
.I file
the answers are read from
.I file
instead (see
.BR likeos-install.conf (5)),
and nothing is asked but the confirmation before the disk is changed, which
.B \-\-yes
gives in advance.
.SS What is installed
Erasing the whole disk gives it a new GUID partition table with two
partitions: an EFI system partition of 512 MiB (FAT32, label LIKEOS-ESP)
and the LikeOS root file system (ext4, label likeos-root) in the rest of
the disk.
Installing on one partition formats that partition with ext4 and uses the
EFI system partition the disk has already (FAT, at least 100 MB; the first
one when there are several).
LikeOS needs at least the size the system image asks for
.RB ( /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst.info ).
.PP
The system image is
.BR /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst ,
checked against its checksum
.RB ( /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst.sha256 )
before it is unpacked.
The installed system gets an
.B /etc/fstab
naming its file systems by UUID, the boot loader in
.B \eEFI\eLIKEOS\eBOOTX64.EFI
(and
.B \eEFI\eBOOT\eBOOTX64.EFI
as the firmware's fallback) on its EFI system partition, and a firmware boot
entry labelled
.B LikeOS
first in the boot order (see
.BR likeos-efiboot (1)).
It starts straight into LikeOS, without the boot menu of the installation
medium.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-answers " file"
Install unattended, with the answers in
.IR file .
.TP
.B \-\-list\-disks
List the disks LikeOS can be installed on, and exit.
The disk the running system was started from cannot be chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Do everything but change the disk: check the answers, work out and show the
plan (partitions, file systems, what is erased), then stop.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not ask for the last confirmation before the disk is changed.
Meant for
.BR \-\-answers ;
it is the caller's confirmation that the disk named there may be erased.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-reboot
Do not restart the computer when the installation is done (the
.B reboot
setting of an answer file is overridden).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show the installer's log lines (each step, each program it runs and its
result) as well as the progress.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-tty
Put the terminal on the standard input back into line mode with echo
(line editing, echo, Ctrl-C and the other signal keys, carriage return
read as newline, newline written as carriage return and newline), and
exit.
An installation turns echo and line mode off and puts them back when it
ends; a
.B likeos-install
that was killed cannot, and the installation medium's console session runs
this before each of its menus.
It fails (exit status 4) when the standard input is not a terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
LikeOS was installed (or, with
.B \-\-dry\-run
or
.BR \-\-list\-disks ,
the plan or the list was shown; with
.BR \-\-reset\-tty ,
the terminal was reset).
.TP
.B not 0
The installation failed or was cancelled, or the command line or the answer
file had a mistake; the reason is shown, and the log says more.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst
The system image that is installed, with its checksum
.RB ( .sha256 )
and a description
.RB ( .info ).
.TP
.B /tmp/likeos-install.log
The log of the installation; a copy is kept on the installed system as
.BR /var/log/likeos-install.log .
.TP
.B /mnt/likeos
Where the new system's file systems are mounted during the installation.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install on /dev/nvme0n1 without questions, erasing it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat > answers.conf <<'EOF'
disk=/dev/nvme0n1
whole_disk=yes
locale=de_DE.UTF\-8
timezone=Europe/Berlin
keyboard=de
hostname=office\-pc
user_fullname="Erika Mustermann"
user_name=erika
user_password_hash=$y$j9T$...
EOF
likeos\-install \-\-answers answers.conf \-\-dry\-run
likeos\-install \-\-answers answers.conf \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
